RARP = Reverse Address Resolution Protocol
It performs MAC address → IP address resolution.
A device that knows its MAC but doesn't know its IP sends a RARP request.
An RARP server maintains the MAC-to-IP mapping and replies with the IP.
It was historically used mainly by diskless computers during boot, but was later replaced by BOOTP and DHCP.

RARP resolves a device's IP address from its MAC address using an RARP server. It was mainly used by diskless computers that did not have a local disk 
